  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P1] Restore tenant scoping in getDocument query",
      "body": "Any authenticated user can now retrieve another tenant's document simply by supplying its ID. The removed line `tenantId: ctx.user.tenantId,` was the only tenant isolation on this query; the surviving filter `where: { id }` (`src/documents.ts:33`, in `getDocument`) performs an ID-only lookup, so `db.documents.findFirst` will match and return documents belonging to other tenants. This is a cross-tenant authorization bypass / data-exposure regression that bites under realistic inputs (any enumerable or leaked document ID) and directly contradicts the PR's stated intent of preserving existing contracts. Restore the tenant filter, e.g. `where: { id, tenantId: ctx.user.tenantId }`.",
      "severity": "P1",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/documents.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 33,
        "end": 33
      }
    }
